Objective of vignette: show way to create the DATRAS part of FishGlob data set.

**Outline:**

1. Load DATRASextra
2. Download data


<!-- The package is loaded into the R environment with: -->

<!-- ```{r} -->
<!-- library(DATRASextra) -->
<!-- ``` -->


<!-- ## *Download DATRAS* -->

<!-- The `downloadDATRAS` function allows us to download information for any of these -->
<!-- surveys. If the arguments `surveys` and `years` are not specified (`NULL`), all -->
<!-- surveys and years are downloaded, wich can take a while. For demonstration -->
<!-- purposes, we download year 2023 of the NS-IBTS survey into a temporary -->
<!-- directory: -->

<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = "", eval = FALSE, cache = TRUE} -->
<!-- tmp <- tempdir() -->
<!-- downloadDATRAS(dir = tmp, year = 2024) -->
<!-- ``` -->


<!-- ## *Read-in DATRAS* -->

<!-- Next, we can read the downloaded survey information into R: -->

<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = "", eval = FALSE} -->
<!-- surv0 <- readDATRAS(file.path(tmp, survey)) -->
<!-- ``` -->


<!-- For demonstration purposes we use the example data set "XXX" that is included in -->
<!-- the DATRASextra package. It represents a tiny subset of the full DATRAS data -->
<!-- base with 2 years and 4 surveys for 5 species. However, this suffices to -->
<!-- demonstrate the main functionality of the package and how to create FishGlob -->
<!-- style dataset. We can load the example data set with: -->

<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = "", eval = TRUE} -->
<!-- data("dab") ## TODO create and use actual data set -->
<!-- ``` -->


<!-- ## *Clean DATRAS* -->


<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = ""} -->
<!-- surv_cleaned <- cleanFishglob(surv0)  ## TODO (in R/fishglob.R) -->
<!-- ``` -->


<!-- Alternatively (maybe not necessary to mention in vignette?) or in extra section -->
<!-- in end to avoid confusion? -->

<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = "", eval = FALSE} -->
<!-- surv_cleaned <- clean(surv0, do.fishglob = TRUE) -->
<!-- ``` -->



<!-- ## *Get Weight by haul* -->

<!-- ```{r, fig.alt = "", eval = FALSE} -->
